n-open game whose identifier the caller never learns. A single combined creation act with prevalidation and encoding before the sole Append is the accepted shape; legacy create@0 and name@0 judgments preserved, binding version bumped accordingly. Where a read can still fail after the record is durable, the record identifier is surfaced rather than discarded. A regression written from desired behaviour, demonstrated to fail against the unrepaired code, covering the maximum-bound case and proving exactly one named game, one effective naming judgment, and stable replay. (2) The two constant assertions in TestCreateV0JudgmentsRemainCompatibleInBothDirections are cut or made to assert what their comment promises; if the create path changes, the hand-rolled legacyDecision is re-verified against the real v0 behaviour. (3) README documents the fold-version bump, the naming act, and that existing repositories become unopenable, describing the end state a reader meets. (4) The lobby derives its open/restricted copy from the admission predicate rather than seat emptiness. The three blockers closed under 96f5989b remain closed. Full gates green at the exact head with -count=1 including -race. Ten exact paths republished at the delivered head, then a fresh independent review requested from an actor other than yourself. Do not merge, and do not review or circulate b07107ab.","severity":"high","to":"09c97907402e7747d051c0c599d9eb463c48d19825820a3e4c433cde2e60e2a8"}}